<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        The <a href="/dmx">DMX Desk</a> controls the venue's lighting through a kiosk's DMX output. It needs the
        Admin or CanManageDmxSystems role. Start by choosing the kiosk (client) whose lights you want to control.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="The desk">
        <ul>
            <li>Each slider is one DMX channel. Drag it to set the level.</li>
            <li><strong>Group by Fixture</strong> groups the sliders by light. <strong>Show all channels</strong> lists them
                in order, with unpatched channels (ones no fixture uses) at the end.</li>
            <li><strong>Fixture Preview</strong> shows each light as a coloured light on screen, so you can see a scene
                without being in the room.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Blind editing">
        <FluentText>
            With <strong>Blind Editing Mode</strong> on, you can change a scene without the real lights following.
            Turning it off makes the desk drive the lights live, and stops any scenes running on that kiosk so
            they don't fight you for the channels.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Which output the kiosk uses">
        <FluentText>
            On <a href="/manage/clients">Clients</a>, open the kiosk's <strong>Settings</strong>, go to the
            <strong>DMX</strong> tab and pick the device under <strong>Use this Device</strong>.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
